66.0,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":373.8},{"anio":2013,"racha_sat":8,"racha_rnl":16,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":278.6,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":282.1},{"anio":2014,"racha_sat":9,"racha_rnl":12,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":210.5,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":207.1},{"anio":2015,"racha_sat":23,"racha_rnl":20,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":113.8,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":109.0},{"anio":2016,"racha_sat":10,"racha_rnl":11,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":253.8,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":256.9},{"anio":2017,"racha_sat":10,"racha_rnl":11,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":376.4,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":372.5},{"anio":2018,"racha_sat":21,"racha_rnl":21,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":178.4,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":183.4},{"anio":2019,"racha_sat":9,"racha_rnl":8,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":219.6,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":220.8},{"anio":2020,"racha_sat":7,"racha_rnl":7,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":308.6,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":309.6},{"anio":2021,"racha_sat":8,"racha_rnl":13,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":436.7,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":432.0},{"anio":2022,"racha_sat":7,"racha_rnl":4,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":370.1,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":364.6},{"anio":2023,"racha_sat":7,"racha_rnl":9,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":404.5,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":404.5},{"anio":2024,"racha_sat":9,"racha_rnl":9,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":273.9,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":281.2},{"anio":2025,"racha_sat":18,"racha_rnl":20,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_sat_mm":292.0,"lluvia_15jun_31ago_rnl_mm":297.8}]}],"limites":["«sat» y «rnl» no son independientes: las dos reparten el mismo total de cada péntada de CHIRPS y solo difieren en cómo lo reparten entre los días (readme del CHC). Coincidir no valida la racha seca; solo dice que no depende del reparto elegido.","Ninguna de las dos es una medición diaria en tierra. ERA5 (~0.25°) e IMERG (0.1°) se interpolan a la malla de 0.05°: el reparto diario no tiene detalle de 5 km.","Cuando ERA5 o IMERG marcan cero en toda la péntada y CHIRPS no, el CHC reparte el total por igual entre los días; eso puede crear días húmedos artificiales que cortan una racha seca.","Los días van en hora UTC, no en hora de Guatemala. El corte (> 15 días con < 2 mm, 15 jun-31 ago) es el del motor y no se tocó para esta prueba.","Solo cambia la lluvia de junio a agosto; el resto del año y la temperatura son los mismos en las dos series. El resultado no entra en ningún puntaje, ni en la confianza ni en el audio: el semáforo publicado sigue usando «sat».","Las parcelas son puntos de ejemplo elegidos con satélite, no verificados en campo."],"limites_en":["“sat” and “rnl” are not independent: both split the same CHIRPS pentad total and differ only in how they spread it across days (CHC readme). Agreement does not validate the dry spell; it only says the result does not depend on the split chosen.","Neither is a daily ground measurement. ERA5 (~0.25°) and IMERG (0.1°) are interpolated to the 0.05° grid: the daily split has no 5 km detail.","When ERA5 or IMERG is zero for the whole pentad and CHIRPS is not, the CHC spreads the total evenly across the days, which can create artificial wet days that break a dry spell.","Days are UTC calendar days, not Guatemala local time. The cut-off (> 15 days under 2 mm, 15 Jun-31 Aug) is the engine's and was not changed for this test.","Only June-August rainfall changes; the rest of the year and temperature are the same in both series. The result does not enter any score, the confidence or the audio: the published traffic light still uses “sat”.","The plots are example points chosen with satellite data, not verified in the field."]}}